      "id": 1,
      "text": "Jacob Miller built a sawmill in 1838 on a Des Plaines tributary, naming the stream Mill Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Mill_Creek%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A Chicago, Milwaukee, St. Paul train station opened in Old Mill Creek in 1873, linking the village to the regional rail network.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Mill_Creek%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Old Mill Creek became an incorporated village in 1959, formalizing its local government after decades of unincorporated growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Mill_Creek%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The village’s oldest headstone dates back to 1826, predating the sawmill and hinting at early settlement activity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Mill_Creek%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1850 land was bought to build a cemetery, and by 1883 nearly 80 remains were relocated to their current resting place.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Mill_Creek%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
